What it is: the DFlash 2 block-diffusion draft model (5 layers, bf16, 1,924,404,480 parameters, 81 tensors) for
Qwen3.8-27B. It has no embedding table and no lm_head of its own: it uses the target model's (the paper, section
4.2 "Shared embedding and LM head"). Architecture as read from config.json, the safetensors header and the paper:
~/handoffs/2026-10-19-cascade-dflash-drafter.md.
Why the full-precision one: the Chisel NVFP4 build (yuanlin2004/Qwen3.8-27B-Chisel-DFlash2-NVFP4-drafter, rev
57697fc07c2f7e6475017afbba088caa6cce4a6c, 1.36 GB, Apache-2.0, model.safetensors sha256
8d464c9f597c41a2e8917c585454239be14f254592f114675fd9d5d5dbc92f4c) is a weight-format change of this same checkpoint
(compressed-tensors NVFP4A16, group 16, FP8 scales). We keep the bf16 original as the CPU reference and quantize
ourselves for the chip. Not downloaded.

